{"name":"Tall Poppy","hex":"#853534","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tall poppy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A conspicuously successful person, especially one who attracts envious hostility.","Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see tall,‎ poppy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tall_poppy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tall Poppy","blocks":[{"text":"Tall Poppy  was a Japanese Thoroughbred racehorse and broodmare. In 2007 she took the JRA Award for Best Two-Year-Old Filly after winning two of her four races including the Hanshin Juvenile Fillies. In the following year she ran second in the Tulip Sho before recording her biggest win in the Yushun Himba. She finished unplaced in seven subsequent races and was retired from racing in 2010."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Tall_Poppy_20080413P1.jpg/330px-Tall_Poppy_20080413P1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tall_Poppy","wikidata":"Q11322448"},{"title":"Tall poppy syndrome","blocks":[{"text":"Tall poppy syndrome is a term that originated in Australia and New Zealand in the 1980s that refers to people with notable public success or achievements that are ostracised by others as a form of egalitarianism. Intense scrutiny and criticism of such a person is termed as \"cutting down the tall poppy\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Lawrence_Alma-Tadema_11.jpeg/330px-Lawrence_Alma-Tadema_11.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tall_poppy_syndrome","wikidata":"Q1045259"},{"title":"Poppy","blocks":[{"text":"A poppy is a flowering plant in the subfamily Papaveroideae of the family Papaveraceae. Poppies are herbaceous plants, often grown for their colourful flowers. One species of poppy, Papaver somniferum, is the source of the narcotic drug mixture opium, which contains powerful medicinal alkaloids such as morphine and has been used since ancient times as an analgesic and narcotic medicinal and recreational drug. It also produces edible seeds. Following the trench warfare in the poppy fields of Flanders, Belgium, during World War I, poppies, specifically the red poppy, have become a symbol of remembrance of soldiers who have died during wartime, especially in the UK, Canada, Australia, Africa and other Commonwealth realms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Poppies_in_the_Sunset_on_Lake_Geneva.jpg/330px-Poppies_in_the_Sunset_on_Lake_Geneva.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poppy","wikidata":"Q967457"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Katsuhiko-Sumii20110116.jpg/500px-Katsuhiko-Sumii20110116.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Katsuhiko-Sumii20110116.jpg/500px-Katsuhiko-Sumii20110116.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tall Poppy's trainer Katsuhiko Sumii","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKatsuhiko-Sumii20110116.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/A_bright_red_poppy_flower.jpg/500px-A_bright_red_poppy_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/A_bright_red_poppy_flower.jpg/1280px-A_bright_red_poppy_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/A_bright_red_poppy_flower.jpg/500px-A_bright_red_poppy_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A close-up of a red-flowered poppy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File